{"question_text": {"৪৮তম বিশেষ বিসিএস [স্বাস্থ্য] – মেডিকেল অংশ": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which is the most common cause of acute retention of urine in male? ", "option1": "Phimosis ", "option2": "Urethral stricture ", "option3": "Bladder outlet obstruction", "option4": "Acute prostatitis ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_399457745431750568159557.png\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) What is the standard urethral catheter size for adult male for uncomplicated catheterization? ", "option1": "12 Fr", "option2": "14 Fr", "option3": "16 Fr", "option4": "18 Fr ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_310580602431750579657191.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which is the most common pathogen responsible for acute epididymo-orchitis? ", "option1": "Neisseria gonorrhoeae", "option2": "Chlamydia trachomatis ", "option3": "Escherichia coli", "option4": "Ureaplasma urelyticum", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_505111003431750581298501.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Which is the most common cause of testicular torsion in adolescents? ", "option1": "High investement of tunica vaginalis ", "option2": "Inversion of the testis ", "option3": "Separation of the epididymis from testis", "option4": "Persistent processus vaginalis ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_789478462431750581580862.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) For testicular salvage, surgery in testicular torsion should be performed within- ", "option1": "12 hours ", "option2": "8 hours ", "option3": "4 hours ", "option4": "6 hours ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_194216732431750582174715.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which is not a cause of phimosis in adults? ", "option1": "Urinary tract infection ", "option2": "Lichen sclerosis ", "option3": "Posthitis ", "option4": "Balanitis ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_375550327431750588389683.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Which is not a recognised treatment option for paraphimosis? ", "option1": "Injection of hyaluronidase ", "option2": "Ventral slit of prepuce ", "option3": "Circumcision ", "option4": "Gentle manual compression", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_740140524431750589411200.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Which is not a component of Virchow's triad? ", "option1": "Thrombophilia", "option2": "Stasis", "option3": "Endothelial injury ", "option4": "Thrombocytopenia", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_179541056431750589702517.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) The risk of thrombosis is increased by- ", "option1": "Exercise ", "option2": "Factor-V Leiden ", "option3": "Antithrombin-III", "option4": "Protein-C ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_102047777431750590269749.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which is the following tests is most sensitive to rule out DVT? ", "option1": "APTT", "option2": "Prothrombin time ", "option3": "Platelet count ", "option4": "D-dimer ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_246546390431750590497843.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which is the first line treatment for established deep vein thrombosis? ", "option1": "Warfarin ", "option2": "Low molecular weight heparin ", "option3": "Rivaroxaban ", "option4": "Dabigatran ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_893769002441750590930119.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_990849127431750590924301.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Extradural hematoma is most commonly caused by rupture of the-", "option1": "Superficial temporal artery ", "option2": "Accessory meningeal artery ", "option3": "Middle meningeal artery ", "option4": "Bridging dural veins ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_884135420431750591210676.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Which is the ideal treatment option for acute subdural hemorrhage? ", "option1": "Burr hole surgery ", "option2": "Craniotomy ", "option3": "Conservative ", "option4": "Calcium channel blockers ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_310412716431750591417106.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) A major head injury is defined as- ", "option1": "GCS <10 ", "option2": "GCS 3-8 ", "option3": "GCS <5 ", "option4": "GCS 9-13", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_707553166431750592090865.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Which is an indication of performing CT within 1 hour of head injury? ", "option1": "More than one episode of vomiting ", "option2": "Age >65 years ", "option3": "Fall from height ", "option4": "Retrograde amnesia >30 minutes ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_450932755431750592254919.png\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Which is the most common cause of acute osteomyelitis in children? ", "option1": "Streptococcus pyogenes ", "option2": "Kingella kingae ", "option3": "Staphylococcus aureus ", "option4": "Streptococcus pneumonae ", "answer": "3", "exp": "Most common organism for acute osteomyelitis in all settings and all age groups is Staphylococcus aureus.<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_451990776431750592616611.jpg\" />", "is_audio": true, "question_duration": "00:00", "answer_duration": "00:02", "explain_duration": "00:00"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Which is the imaging of choice acute osteomyelitis? ", "option1": "Plain radiograph ", "option2": "Ultrasound ", "option3": "CT scan ", "option4": "MRI", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_294925767431750592725647.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Which is the gold standard investigation for diagnosis of achalasia cardia? ", "option1": "Endoluminal ultrasound ", "option2": "Ambulatory pH recording ", "option3": "High resolution manometry ", "option4": "Upper GI endoscopy ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_386600927431750592853495.png\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Which is the most common type of hiatus hernia? ", "option1": "Sliding hernia ", "option2": "Mixed hernia ", "option3": "Rolling hernia ", "option4": "Herniation of small intestine ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_548463878431750593145939.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Which part of the GIT is most commonly affected by peptic ulcer? ", "option1": "Lesser curvature of the stomach ", "option2": "Meckel's diverticulum ", "option3": "Intestinal stomas ", "option4": "First part of duodenum ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_373361327431750593234024.png\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Which is the first line investigation for suspected hollow viscus perforation? ", "option1": "Supine abdominal radiograph ", "option2": "Ultrasound of the abdomen ", "option3": "Endoscopy ", "option4": "Erect chest radiograph ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_204148723431750593343323.png\" />"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Metabolic finding not consisten with gastric outlet obstruction is- ", "option1": "Hypochloremia ", "option2": "Metabolic alkalosis ", "option3": "Hypokalaemia ", "option4": "Production of alkaline urine ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_821503832491750593464745.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) The vomiting in gastric outlet obstruction-", "option1": "is non projectile ", "option2": "contains digested food", "option3": "has no bile ", "option4": "is scanty ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_536472273431750601275331.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Which is the most common cause of intestinal obstruction? ", "option1": "Foreign bodies ", "option2": "Strictures ", "option3": "Adhesions ", "option4": "Malignancy ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_966023604431750601303507.png\" />"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Which is the earliest feature of large gut obstruction? ", "option1": "Abdominal distension ", "option2": "Vomiting ", "option3": "Abdominal pain ", "option4": "Absolute constipation ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_227065892431750601344932.png\" />"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Which is a risk factor for squamous cell carcinoma of esophagus? ", "option1": "Gastroesophageal reflux disease ", "option2": "Smoking ", "option3": "Barret's esophagus ", "option4": "Obesity ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_418098227441750601389574.png\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Which organ is most commonly affected by hematogenous spread from Ca. stomach? ", "option1": "Lung ", "option2": "Liver ", "option3": "Pancreas ", "option4": "Transverse colon ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_817759328431750601444858.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Which of the followings is associated with increased risk of gastric cancer? ", "option1": "Gastric adenomatous polyp ", "option2": "Hyperplastic gastric polyp ", "option3": "Aspirin ", "option4": "Excess fibre in diet ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_514065242431750601480288.png\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Which is the most common etiological factor for hepatocellular carcinoma? ", "option1": "Alcohol consumption ", "option2": "Hepatitis-C ", "option3": "Primary biliary cirrhosis ", "option4": "Hepatitis-B ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_311018004431750601531774.png\" />"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Mutation in which gene is responsible for familial adenomatous polyposis?", "option1": "FAP ", "option2": "BRCA1", "option3": "HER2", "option4": "APC", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_640046286431750601574116.png\" />"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) Which is the most common site of colorectal cancer? ", "option1": "Sigmoid colon", "option2": "Rectum ", "option3": "Left colic flexure ", "option4": "Ascending colon ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_807119946431750601599459.png\" />"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Which is the most common site of distant metastasis from renal cell carcinoma? ", "option1": "Lumbar vertebra ", "option2": "Brain ", "option3": "Lungs ", "option4": "Liver ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_251257468431750601683293.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Which is the most common type of bladder cancer? ", "option1": "Squamous cell carcinoma ", "option2": "Adenocarcinoma ", "option3": "Transitional cell carcinoma ", "option4": "Clear cell carcinoma ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_226774108431750601716239.png\" />"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) Which is the earliest symptom of rectal cancer? ", "option1": "Tenesmus ", "option2": "Per-rectal bleeding ", "option3": "Early morning diarrhoea ", "option4": "Proctitis ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_926590921431750601743807.png\" />"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) Which is the most common risk factor for cholangiocarcinoma? ", "option1": "Clonorchis sinensis ", "option2": "Choledochal cyst ", "option3": "Budd-Chiari syndrome ", "option4": "Primary sclerosing cholangitis ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_687592941431750601771871.png\" />"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) Which of the following arteries does not supply the Little's area of the nasal septum? ", "option1": "Anterior ethmoidal artery ", "option2": "Posterior ethmoidal artery ", "option3": "Sphenopalatine artery ", "option4": "Greater palatine artery ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_755981337431750601799503.png\" />"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) Which is a common cause of epistaxis in the elderly? ", "option1": "Noise picking ", "option2": "Foreign body", "option3": "Anticoagulant therapy ", "option4": "Juvenile angiofibroma ", "answer": "3", "exp": "The most common site of bleeding is from Kiesselbach&rsquo;s plexus in Little&rsquo;s area of the anterior portion of the septum.<br /><br /><em><strong>Anterior bleeding is common in children and young adults owing to nose blowing or picking. </strong></em><br /><br /><em><strong>In the elderly, anticoagulants and hypertension are the underlying causes of arterial bleeding </strong></em><em><strong>from the posterior part of the nose.</strong></em>"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) Which artery is commonly ligated in persistent epistaxis after failed anterior and posterior nasal packing? ", "option1": "Sphenopalatine artery ", "option2": "Greater palatine artery ", "option3": "External carotid artery ", "option4": "Maxillary artery ", "answer": "1", "exp": "Postnasal packing may be required in refractory cases whereby a gauze pack is positioned in the nasopharynx under general anaesthesia. <br /><br /><strong><em>Endoscopic sphenopalatine artery clipping</em> is an effective treatment for signifcant epistaxis not responding to direct cautery or nasal packing.<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_555176626491750603443026.jpg\" /><br /></strong>"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) Which is the most common cause of upper GI bleeding? ", "option1": "Ulcer ", "option2": "Mallory-Weiss tear", "option3": "Ruptured esophageal varices ", "option4": "Esophageal erosion ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_917622317431750603470055.png\" />"}, {"id": "40", "question": "৪০) Which is not true regarding symptoms of hemorrhoids? ", "option1": "Pruritus ", "option2": "Painful", "option3": "Bright red bleeding", "option4": "Mucus discharge", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_971688574431750603498661.png\" />"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 11522, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "1200000", "is_omr": true, "omr_time": "1440000", "examname": "Jun 23, 2025", "type": "BCS-Health-Medic", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}